Z||000034||Tina||12-05-2000||06:45 PM||||Started out with 2 1/4 and reverse mount glasspacks (By accident, not enough sleep)<BR>Actually not bad, but kept blowing the seams of the block-huggers.<BR>With the Exhaustwrap on, actually a cool way of making confetti. But did you know that exhaustwrap voids warranty's.<BR>When the new headers came,(Sanderson)we switched  to 2 for about a week. "Horrid" Whistled like it was breathing through a pair of straws. <BR>So we went the other way. 2 1/2 straight pipe only.<BR>Holy cow, starting it in the detached garage 10 feet away from the house it, still made the window glass of my house vibrate and the dishes shake in the cubboards.<BR>Too much for the daily Driver it is in the summer.<BR>So for right now I, got 2 1/2 from headers to glasspacks and then reduced to 2 1/4.<BR>Chrome tips are still somewhwere in the garage,havn't yet made up my mind if I want to keep it that way.<BR>The sound hard to explain,idles like a 70 <BR>muscle/car. Step on it and the secondary kicks in, better have your earplugs if your behind me.<P>Tina<P>Fiero Pic's at <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/Albumlist?u=1315468" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/Albumlist?u=1315468</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by Tina (edited 12-05-2000).]||||reg||1
